<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Expanding a binomial using the pattern</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Expand \({@brs@}\).</p><div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>The powers of the first term go down, the powers of the second term go up, and every term has total power \({@n@}\). The coefficients for power \({@n@}\) are {@crow@}. Put \(a = {@px@}\) and \(b = {@q@}\) into each term, with brackets:</p><p>\[{@patt@}\]</p><p>Working out each term gives \({@ta@}\)[[if test="is(o=1)"]], which can also be written in ascending powers of \(x\), starting with the constant \({@q^n@}\)[[/if]].</p><p>Check: putting \(x = 1\) gives \(({@p1q@})^{@n@} = {@chk@}\) on both sides.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[validate_x(ex) := if every(lambda([v], is(v=x)), listofvars(ex)) then "" else "Use only the letter x.";
/* Design: expand (a + kx)^n. Source: adapted from SMP AS/A2 Core 2, Chapter 5, Exercise A, question 3. */
L: [[2,5,3,0],[3,-2,4,1],[2,-1,4,0],[3,1,3,1],[2,-3,4,0],[3,2,3,0],[3,4,3,1],[3,-4,4,0],[2,-3,3,1],[3,2,4,1]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
p: L[ix][1];
q: L[ix][2];
n: L[ix][3];
o: L[ix][4];
np1: n+1;
brs: if o=0 then sconcat("\\left(",p,"x",if q>0 then "+" else "-",abs(q),"\\right)^{",n,"}") else sconcat("\\left(",q,"+",p,"x\\right)^{",n,"}");
ta: expand((p*x+q)^n);
fresh: p^n*x^n+q^n;
notpow: sum(binomial(n,r)*p*x^(n-r)*q^r,r,0,n-1)+q^n;
flip: expand((p*x-q)^n);
chk: (p+q)^n;
crow: if n=3 then "1, 3, 3, 1" else "1, 4, 6, 4, 1";
px: p*x;
pnxn: p^n*x^n;
pxn: p*x^n;
p2x2: p^2*x^2;
p1q: p+q;
bpw(s,k) := if k=0 then "" else if k=1 then sconcat("\\left(",s,"\\right)") else sconcat("\\left(",s,"\\right)^{",k,"}");
patt: simplode(makelist(sconcat(if r=0 or r=n then "" else string(binomial(n,r)),bpw(sconcat(p,"x"),n-r),bpw(string(q),r)),r,0,n)," + ");
terms: makelist(binomial(n,r)*(p*x)^(n-r)*q^r,r,0,n);]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
  <specificfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></specificfeedback>
  <questionnote format="moodle_auto_format">
    <text>ix={@ix@}, p={@p@}, q={@q@}, n={@n@}, o={@o@}, ta={@ta@}</text>
  </questionnote>
  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Binomial Expansions: expanding using the pattern</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 1.2: Expand (px + q)^n or (q + px)^n, n = 3 or 4, by substituting into the pattern of (a + b)^n.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Chapter 5, Section A, Exercise A, question 3 of Cassell, D., Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Core 2 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2004: new expressions and powers, randomised; the pattern of (a + b)^n is used with brackets round each substituted term.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
